Attribution
================================================================

CC BY 4.0 requires attribution. I'm not strict about the exact
wording — the spirit is what matters:

  1. Credit "pawa" (or "pawa / pawagit") as the author.
  2. Link back to the source repository:
     https://github.com/pawagit/mushroom-species-icons
  3. Indicate the license (the string "CC BY 4.0" is enough;
     a link to https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
     is even better).
  4. If you modified the icons, say so briefly
     (e.g. "recoloured", "simplified further", "cropped").

Examples of attributions that work:

  - In a credits page or about screen:

      Mushroom icons by pawa, CC BY 4.0
      https://github.com/pawagit/mushroom-species-icons

  - Inline on a map or figure caption:

      Icons: pawa (CC BY 4.0)

  - In a README or docs file:

      Mushroom species icons are by pawa and used under
      CC BY 4.0. Source:
      https://github.com/pawagit/mushroom-species-icons

Attribution does not need to be on every page or next to every
icon — a single visible credit (credits page, footer, about
dialog, README, etc.) for the project that uses the icons is
fine.

If the medium genuinely can't carry an attribution (e.g. an
embroidered patch), do your best in whatever accompanying
material exists, or get in touch.
